Subject: [PATCH] docs: git channel contract, STATUS, budget, enforced
 isolation

Answers the three doubts raised in channel message 0002:

1. Invariant 7 now says isolation is enforced by code rather than by
   model compliance: plugin-level capability composition and guards by
   default, system-level isolation as an optional layer. Reverse
   isolation is detection-only at the plugin level.
2. Adds the STATUS type for heartbeats and state, and defines budget as
   max_hours and max_rounds, metered by each side for itself.
3. Replaces the unowned channel server with a git-repo channel. The full
   contract lives in docs/channel-git.md, including relay mode.

Also requires lg-global to be installed only into a dedicated profile.

